WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.810
- One of my favorite moments
from the whole thing,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.150
was when she just flat out asked you,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.980
because you had said, "One
of the gutsiest things,"

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.487
she'd asked you a
question, you said, "Hey,

00:00:09.487 --> 00:00:10.860
"one of the gutsiest
things I've ever done"

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.240
was staying in your marriage

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.760
when no one expected you to.
- Yeah.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.300
I used to be a very private person.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.747
That all ended when,

00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:21.120
(audience laughing mildly)
I ended up in public life.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.140
- Yeah-
- And,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.700
I know, because-
- So fun!

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.080
- I know, because I've now,
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.000
you know, lived a long time.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.280
Everybody goes through something.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.980
I mean relationships
which are at the core,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.160
of who you are and how you define,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.300
the meaning in your life,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.160
everybody goes through something.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.830
And not everybody, like you
or me, does it in public.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.510
But everybody goes through it.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.460
And so if we can,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.730
and you've done such a important service

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.580
in being open and
talking, and sharing that.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.017
And so, for me to be able to say,

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:56.707
"Look, everybody has to make
the decision that's best

00:00:56.707 --> 00:01:01.050
"for her or him, and it's not
gonna be the same decision."

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.910
- 'Cause we're all different-
- We're all different.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.830
- And nobody knows the whole relationship-

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.204
- Nobody-
- In the scope of your life.

00:01:06.204 --> 00:01:07.037
- Knows-
- Yeah.

00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:08.220
- And we need to respect that,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.690
if it's a responsible decision.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.460
I mean, you know,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.810
I know people who, you know,
they can't make a decision

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.240
because they're still not
clear in their own heads

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.170
how to best manage what
they are in right now,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.230
and how to get out of it
or how to, make it better.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.540
But, you gotta go through the process.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.340
You can't short-circuit the process.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.173
- Yeah.
- And so when you say,

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:32.730
"Yeah, you've been going
through it," you do.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:37.230
And you know, for me, it took
a lot of, thought and prayer,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.460
and trusted friends and
confidants to talk to,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.920
and really, think through out loud,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.440
and I, you know, I made
the right decision for me.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.640
I have no regrets.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.010
And so I want everybody to feel that way.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.440
And, that doesn't mean that it's perfect

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.810
'cause nothing in life is, but,

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.790
you do the best you
can and then you go on.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.790
And that's what we should be looking to.

